  "context": "2026-11-03: spec clause and double-generation finding added; overlaps the fallback row-count sites in perf-arrow-aware-result-capture-20261030 (same files), so that item waits on this one. Origin: root-cause analysis of RF1 timing and its adversarial review. [INFERENCE] query generation cost may explain the uniform +1 to +2 ms per-query shifts in t3-perf-execution-variants-regression-20261010.\n\n2026-11-03 correction round: need on the reference page removed so the fix is not delayed by documentation; ADR reconciliation gate and closing steps added.\n\n2026-11-05: implemented option A (query-generation slice of timing method 2; timing_method untouched; separation by BenchBox version and changelog). Owner A/B/C choice still pending; quote it here before the PR is armed. DuckDB TPC-H SF0.01 power run: per-query median 9.7 ms before, 1.4 ms after (3 runs each). Closing steps owed at merge: update result-schema-2-4-producer-20261022 (if A) and set not_before on perf-smoke-rebaseline-after-power-query-generation-20261103.\n\n2026-11-06 owner decision (Joe, answering a choice dialog about PR #3960): \"A\". So this change is the query-generation part of timing method 2 in the locality ADR. timing_method stays unwritten, and the BenchBox version plus the changelog separate the results until result-schema-2-4-producer-20261022 lands.",
  "description": "Problem. In the TPC-H power test (benchbox/core/tpch/power_test.py) query_start is taken before benchmark.get_query(...), which runs a qgen subprocess (tpch/queries.py) plus dialect translation; the TPC-DS power test (benchbox/core/tpcds/power_test.py) does the same with dsqgen. The throughput tests pregenerate text (tpch/throughput_test.py _resolve_query_text), so the two tests time different work. Measured on one macOS host: get_query takes a median 5.1 ms per query at steady state (first call 376 ms), against perf-smoke baseline queries of 4.4 to 12.3 ms, so power numbers carry roughly the generation cost per query and skew fast engines. It affects 22 of the 24 Power@Size terms for TPC-H and the corresponding TPC-DS terms.\n\nSpec: TPC-H 3.0.1 clause 5.3.7.2 defines a query interval from submission of the query to the SUT; query generation by the driver precedes submission and is not part of it.\n\nAlso: _preflight_validate_generation in the TPC-H power test already calls get_query for every query in the permutation and discards the text, so generation runs twice per query. Generate once, keep the text, and execute that text.\n\nReconciliation with a recorded decision: the accepted locality ADR, amendment 'Round Trip Removed and Platform Timings' (item 6: timers measure only the query; adapters move tag setup, stats lookups, validation, plan capture and power-test query generation out of the measured timer; runs record run.timing_method and are compared and ranked within one method; published numbers change when the timer fix lands), and the open item result-schema-2-4-producer-20261022 already cover this scope. The ADR moved to the site repository in #3545; its pre-move text is docs/development/adr/adr-client-link-locality-disclosure.md at commit e4a8a09091^. This item is the query-generation slice of that work.\n\nDECISION GATE (owner, before the PR is armed): how bundles produced after this change are told apart from earlier ones. (A, recommended) Land as the query-generation slice of timing method 2; timing_method stays unwritten by this item (the code reads it but no producer writes it; method 2 requires every scope in the ADR to be out of the timer), and separation until result-schema-2-4-producer lands relies on the BenchBox version recorded in the bundle plus the changelog; result-schema-2-4-producer then needs this item and drops query generation from its timer-scope bullet. (B) Add an interim marker field. (C) The owner supersedes ADR item 6 for this slice and accepts changelog-only separation. Only the owner chooses; quote the choice in context. Implementation and tests may proceed before the choice; arming may not.\n\nGuardrails for all code work: work only in a linked worktree (make worktree-create); never edit the primary clone. No explanatory comments or docstrings in source (make comment-policy-check). Durations use benchbox.utils.clock.mono_time()/elapsed_seconds(). Add a changelog.d/ fragment. Cited line numbers are orientation only: re-read the named symbols, docs and spec clauses before editing and treat a mismatch as a reason to stop and update this item. No live-cloud runs without owner approval; heavy runs only through make heavy-run or a lock-taking entry point. Green focused tests are not release certification. The text executed must be byte-identical to today's for the same seed, stream and dialect (power_stream_seed unchanged). A generation error must still abort the run before the first query is timed (preflight semantics). Generation time is not added to any metric input. Do not edit the perf-smoke baseline here; perf-smoke-rebaseline-after-power-query-generation-20261103 owns it.",
  "final_evidence": {
